Return Value
Each function returns the double value produced by interpreting the input characters as a number. The return value is 0.0 if the input cannot be converted to a value of that type.
In Visual C++, in all out-of-range cases, errno is set to ERANGE. If the parameter passed in is NULL, the invalid parameter handler is invoked, as described in Parameter Validation. If execution is allowed to continue, these functions set errno to EINVAL and return 0.
